// Emacs style mode select   -*- C++ -*-
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// DESCRIPTION:
//    Menu font harvested from existing WAD patches - glyph data and drawing
//    routines. See m_thinfont.h for why this exists and
//    tools/gen_thinfont.py for how thinfont_glyphs below was generated.
//
//    Most letters here are forced-capital (C, S, I, T): an earlier lowercase
//    set for s/i/t (borrowed from "sensitivity") was cropped too close to
//    its neighbors and carried a visible sliver of the next letter along,
//    reading as garbled/badly-clipped strokes in game - so those stayed
//    capital-only for a while, which then looked wrong in a different way
//    ("MuSIC", "SeTTIngs": real mid-word capitals standing out next to
//    genuinely lowercase letters). The other letters below (o, n, e, r, g,
//    l, y, p) look shorter than the capitals simply because that's how tall
//    they are in the source patches - this font mixes true word-initial
//    capitals with genuine lowercase letters, matching normal title case.
//
//    find_glyph() below tries the exact character first and only falls back
//    to its uppercase fold if that's missing, so a handful of letters (i, s,
//    t, c, h, a) now have real lowercase entries sourced from clean
//    mid-title lowercase words instead of "sensitivity" - see
//    tools/gen_thinfont.py. 'c' is the one exception to "clean":
//    "Ultra-Violence" is packed tightly enough that no full column gap
//    exists anywhere near it, but the letterform itself (open on the right
//    at mid-height) is unambiguous even where it touches its neighbors,
//    unlike the old s/i/t attempt. h came from "Knee-Deep in the Dead"'s
//    "the" - needed for "Cheats" to read as a normal word instead of
//    all-caps in the Options menu list. a went through two rounds of
//    replacement: first cropped from that title's "Dead" (a ragged,
//    stepped notch out of its bottom-left corner read as a cut-off
//    stroke in game), then re-cropped from "G[a]me" in M_NGAME (see 'm'
//    below, the same word) too narrowly, which this time clipped the
//    bowl's own left curve instead of a neighbor's. The column range
//    finally used (67-80) was confirmed by eye against a full-size
//    render of M_NGAME with the real PLAYPAL palette rather than read
//    off a raw pixel dump - see tools/gen_thinfont.py.
//
//    M/U (from "MOUSE SENSITIVITY") and V (from "SOUND VOLUME") were added
//    for the "Music: Type I/II/..." menu row - any character not in this
//    table silently renders as blank space (see M_WriteThinText).
//
//    'm' is a genuinely lowercase, real-diagonal glyph from "Ga[m]e" in
//    M_NGAME (the main menu's "New Game" graphic) - initially assumed
//    unavailable like 'b'/'f' and handcrafted from straight legs and a
//    bridge instead, but none of those synthesized attempts (three of
//    them) ever read as "M": a real M needs diagonal strokes, which no
//    amount of leg-width or bridge-position tuning can fake with straight
//    verticals. It was found by actually rendering M_NGAME with the real
//    PLAYPAL palette (see tools/gen_thinfont.py's render-to-PNG helper
//    used during that investigation) instead of guessing letter
//    boundaries from raw pixel dumps, which is also worth doing for any
//    future glyph hunt in this table.
//
//    'b' is still not harvested from any WAD patch - no menu graphic in
//    any supported IWAD (DOOM1/DOOM/DOOMU/DOOM2/PLUTONIA/TNT) contains a
//    lowercase or uppercase 'b' cleanly isolated from its neighbors (same
//    goes for 'f', which is why it's still missing). It's handcrafted
//    instead: 'P' flipped top-to-bottom - a stem topped with a bowl
//    becomes a stem with the bowl at the bottom, exactly 'b' (a first
//    attempt spliced 'h''s stem with a mirrored 'c' bowl running the full
//    stem height, which read as 'D', not 'b').
//
//    A separate fix brightens 'R''s cropped left edge to 191 - it
//    anti-aliases dimmer than this font's other stems in the source
//    patch, which reads as a missing stroke when nothing precedes it at
//    the start of a word. See tools/gen_thinfont.py, which reproduces all
//    of the above so regenerating the table doesn't silently drop them.
//
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

